uses.Interesting - chat-send-user-turn always sets Provider and Surface to INTERNAL_MESSAGE_CHANNEL (webchat). So for gateway chat.sends, turnSourceChannel for exec might come from messageProvider which is...So chat-send sets Provider: INTERNAL_MESSAGE_CHANNEL (webchat). That would make turnSourceChannel webchat which is ENABLED for approvals!\nLet me find where messageProvider is set when creating tools for a session - specifically for dashboard sessions.The background says they get initiating-platform-unsupported with dashboard channel. Looking at resolveApprovalInitiatingSurfaceState - if channel is \"dashboard\", it would:Let me look at AgentShell's connection code and how it handles chat/approvals. Also check how messageProvider becomes dashboard - maybe from OriginatingChannel when deliver is true, or from session la...Let me check origin-routing and how Provider/OriginatingChannel can become dashboard. Also need session create validation for custom keys.Important: `isDeliverableMessageChannel` has a subtle check:\nThe subtle part here is that `isDeliverableMessageChannel` in `message-channel-core.ts` is doing a stricter check than the one in `message-channel-normalize.ts`.Looking at TUI session keys - they use keys like `tui-next` which becomes `agent:main:tui-next` via toAgentStoreSessionKey - NOT `agent:main:tui:uuid` with channel segment \"tui\"!\nCritical finding: AgentShell connect uses:AgentShell uses `sessions.send` not `chat.send`! That's a different path. Let me trace sessions.send for messageProvider/channel.Let me read sessions-messaging.ts for how channel is setsessions.send dispatches to chat.send, which sets Provider = webchat. So messageProvider should be webchat for AgentShell path...\nRegardless of whether the exact reason is `initiating-platform-unsupported` vs `no-approval-route`, I have enough to answer the four questions properly. Let me also check a few more tui side effects r...Got it — thanks for the deep dive. That covers the key behavioral differences for TUI vs. other channels pretty cleanly.\n\nQuick summary of what I see:\n\n- TUI is treated as a first-class “initiating surface” in approval flows (exec-approval-surface.ts) and is markdown-capable, but it 100 % relies on the gateway for turn-source forwarding (approval-turn-source.ts returns false for chat forwarding).\n- The session-key channel segment “tui” is purely a hint for lastChannel resolution and does **not** make the messageProvider “tui” unless the originating provider is explicitly TUI. That’s why chat.send still lands as webchat even when the key contains :tui:.\n- Empty channel or missing channel segment falls back to webchat internally, which is why parseAgentSessionKey rejects keys without at least three parts.Let me check resolveEffectiveReplyRouteTUI caps are interesting - let me read the full caps listVery important: TUI does NOT advertise EXEC_APPROVALS - only PLUGIN_APPROVALS! And TUI is only in PLUGIN_APPROVAL_CLIENT_IDS. So how does TUI get exec approvals then?\nSo for chat.send path:\n- Provider = webchatThat dual-gate breakdown is spot-on. The initiating surface check is gated on the `messageProvider` value (which is always `webchat` for the chat.send path), so even if the session key carries a `dashboard` segment, it never reaches the approval surface because the provider is fixed. The `unsupported` label is therefore a red herring here — the real failure is the missing approval route because the client ID is `\"cli\"` and caps are empty.I have a clear picture. Let me also check if session key with just 2 segments can work, and what happens with webchat key segment.\nI found the first-party pattern. Mac app uses clientId: \"openclaw-macos\" which is hard-coded as EXEC_APPROVAL_CLIENT_IDS.\nInteresting - the official macOS app uses clientId \"openclaw-macos\" with caps: [] by default, and relies on the hard-coded EXEC_APPROVAL_CLIENT_IDS set. So AgentShell could either:That makes sense—thanks for laying out the options clearly. The key insight is that `normalizeGatewayClientId` is strict, so we’re locked into the closed set of valid client IDs.Deliver the full output in the required shape.",
